detector_raw:
{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this packing plan — are you trying to minimize the number of containers used, maximize the total weight (or total units) of goods shipped, or is there another goal such as maximizing profit or meeting a specific demand?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice (the objective function) by presenting mutually exclusive options, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the goal is to minimize the number of containers, are you required to ship all available goods (i.e., every unit of A, B, C, D, and E must be loaded), or is it acceptable to leave some goods unshipped as long as the containers that are used satisfy the weight and composition rules?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether all goods must be shipped or if some can be left unshipped. This is a binary policy choice, constituting one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there a fixed number of containers available to choose from, or is the number of containers unlimited (i.e., you can use as many as needed, subject to the per-container rules)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the constraint on the number of containers."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the \"at least 12 units of type D per container\" rule — does this apply to every container that is used, including containers that contain no type D goods at all (which would then be infeasible), or is the intent that any container that contains type D must contain at least 12 units of it?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the scope of the constraint (all containers vs. only those containing type D), which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Does this mean it's acceptable to leave some goods unshipped (i.e., the total shipped can be less than the available amount), or must all available goods be shipped?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy decision regarding whether the constraint is an upper bound (allowing under-shipping) or an equality (requiring full shipment)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Does this mean at least 1 unit of type C, or is there a specific minimum number of type C units required when type A is present?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single clarification regarding the specific minimum quantity of type C units required when type A is present."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are these strict inequalities (i.e., weight must be strictly greater than 18 and strictly less than 60), or are they inclusive (i.e., weight can be exactly 18 or exactly 60)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the weight constraints are strict or inclusive."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the goods types — are the units of each type indivisible (i.e., you can only load whole units, making this an integer problem), or can goods be split fractionally (e.g., 0.5 units of type A)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question about whether goods units are indivisible or splittable, which is one policy choice."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "if the answer turns out to be \"not all goods need to be shipped,\" would the model simply minimize the number of containers while respecting the per-container rules and the upper bounds on each type, with no penalty or requirement for leftover goods?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single compound clarification question about the modeling objective and constraints in a specific scenario, which constitutes one semantically independent request for confirmation."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any upper bound on the number of containers you would realistically consider, or should the model simply find the minimum number of containers needed (which could be as few as 1) subject to all the rules?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy decision regarding the objective function or constraints on the number of containers (upper bound vs. minimization)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "is there any requirement that each container must contain at least one unit of every goods type (A, B, C, D, E), or is it acceptable for a container to contain only a subset of the types (e.g., only D and E, with no A, B, or C)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single structural question about container composition constraints, presenting a binary choice (all types required vs. subset allowed) that constitutes one independent clarification."
}
